            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Product Development & Launch Challenges</b></h3>

                ```
                <p>
                    Moving from product development to a successful market launch can introduce
                    several challenges. Managing these challenges early can help organizations
                    reduce delays, improve product quality, and create a better launch experience.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Changing Requirements:</b> Customer and business requirements can change
                    during development. Maintaining a prioritized product backlog and roadmap
                    helps teams manage changes without losing focus.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Development Delays:</b> Technical dependencies, resource constraints,
                    integration problems, and unexpected defects can affect launch schedules.
                    Regular progress reviews and risk management help teams identify potential
                    delays earlier.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Insufficient Testing:</b> Releasing a product without adequate testing
                    can result in usability problems, performance issues, or functional defects.
                    Comprehensive validation before launch helps reduce these risks.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Poor Launch Coordination:</b> Product, marketing, sales, support, and
                    operations teams need to work from a common launch plan. Clear responsibilities
                    and communication help prevent operational gaps.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Limited Customer Adoption:</b> A technically successful product may still
                    struggle if customers do not understand its value. Clear positioning,
                    onboarding, communication, and customer support can improve adoption.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant challenges image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    ```

