                <h3><b>Product Testing and Launch Readiness</b></h3>

                ```
                <p>
                    Launch readiness requires teams to verify that the product is technically
                    stable and capable of delivering the expected customer experience. Testing
                    should cover the most important product workflows, integrations, and
                    operational scenarios.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Functional testing verifies that product features work according to
                    requirements. Integration testing ensures that connected systems and
                    services communicate correctly. Performance testing can help identify
                    issues that may occur under expected usage conditions.
                </p>

                <p>
                    User acceptance testing also provides an opportunity for representative
                    users or stakeholders to validate important workflows before the product
                    is released to a broader audience.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Validate critical product workflows.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Verify integrations and external dependencies.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Evaluate product performance and reliability.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> Complete user acceptance and launch-readiness testing.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

